                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Tucson AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 14 at 9:11PM MST until September 14 at 11:30PM MST by NWS Tucson AZ",
                "description": "FFWTWC\n\nThe National Weather Service in Tucson has extended the\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNorth Central Pima County in southeastern Arizona...\n\n* Until 1130 PM MST.\n\n* At 911 PM MST, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms had produced heavy rain in Brawley Wash at Manville\nRoad. Between 1.5 and 2.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nAvra Valley, Saguaro National Park West and Picture Rocks.\n\nThis includes the following Flash Flood Prone Locations...\nManville Rd at Brawley Wash and Twin Peaks Rd between Sanders and\nSandario.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
